h god-like powers  on top of all that  aaron also managed to get the warhammer  titan power  so now it's clear that him coming into  contact with zeke  was the most important part of the plan  and whether they got the jaw titan armor  titan  wasn't actually that important people  mentioned the lives that were sacrificed  to get aaron back but again you could  say everyone's life would have been  sacrificed if he didn't do this  eventually  now much of marlene technology has been  destroyed and they have the rumbling of  the colossal  titans they can use if the merlions try  anything aaron has definitely increased  the likelihood of island ld and survival  through this mission but let me know  your thoughts do you blame aaron for the  deaths that happened including sasha's  or do you think aaron had to do it  anyways connie comes and confirms the  really tragic truth that sasha is dead  he cries armin cries mikasa cries and  aaron two  is crushed her last word was meat  she tried to keep them laughing right  until the end but she won't be able to  do that anymore  again symbolizing a shift in the series  to a much darker tone  where there is even less space for  comedic relief like the kind sasha  always offered us  through the flashback we see that sasha  was a very positive optimistic person  but as i said  in the attack on titan world so far it  seems like the good pure ones die young  while the others get corrupted and  arguably even become villains  if you ask the marleans our protagonist  aaron has just become the biggest  worst villain in the world again people  even blame sasha's death on aaron saying  she only died because aaron dragged the  scouts into this but no one says that he  may  have saved everyone else it wasn't an  easy decision for aaron but as the  preview of the next episode  says unable to change the past they must  continue down the one before them  if you haven't read the manga and didn't  see the death coming let me know how  sasha's death 